{
  "storyId": "B-cc10",
  "name": "proof-or-stop-path-and-package-identity-migration",
  "title": "Migrate the remaining lattice identities: bin aliases, state dirs, config filenames, and npm package name",
  "description": "B-cdf6 renamed the user-facing CLI to proof-or-stop but deliberately FROZE six identities because renaming them orphans live state or breaks resolution by exact name. This story retires all six. (1) Remove bin/lattice.js and bin/lattice-codex.js, ending the deprecated-bin compatibility window. (2) .lattice -> .proof-or-stop state directory (7571 git-tracked files). (3) .lattice-codex -> .proof-or-stop-codex adapter directory. (4) lattice.config.json -> proof-or-stop.config.json. (5) lattice.json -> proof-or-stop.json manifest. (6) @lattice/core -> @proof-or-stop/core npm package name across 4 package.json manifests plus lockfiles. Verified precondition: the signature salts (lattice-*-integrity-v1) are standalone string constants independent of any path or filename, so renaming paths does NOT invalidate historical signatures; the salts stay frozen as separate literals. The hard problem is not find-and-replace, it is migrating live on-disk state and preserving 326 story archives without rewriting frozen history.",
